title: stop the server later if you want
pid: e855edbf-9aa1-47d2-bd71-826df35c0578
body: |2-
  Run the stop script, giving it the config you gave the start script
  (by default, as for the start script, data/jeff/skgconfig.toml):
  #+begin_example
     bash/stop-servers.sh [CONFIG]
  #+end_example
  It runs the stop script that the start wrote in the run folder
  (data/jeff/skgconfig.toml.running/stop-servers.sh for the default
  config), after checking that its PID still names that start.

  You can't use the client (much) when the server isn't running.
